 increase.", "grounded": ["oms.S20-S01.span0"], "n_grounded": 1, "note": ""}, {"fault_mode": "WSS_PORT_FAIL", "location_kind": "shared", "term": null, "anchor_symptom": null, "anchor_service": null, "element": "E1", "probability": 0.02, "rationale": "A WSS port failure at the common S20 ROADM could interrupt many channels and therefore the affected services. It would not normally cause OSC loss on both fibres of two external spans, which strongly argues against it.", "grounded": ["roadm.S20"], "n_grounded": 1, "note": ""}, {"fault_mode": "CONNECTOR_PULLED", "location_kind": "term", "term": "oms_input", "anchor_symptom": "O1", "anchor_service": null, "element": null, "probability": 0.01, "rationale": "A disconnected S20 OMS input could cause downstream loss on one outgoing direction. It does not explain the paired reverse-direction OSC losses or the simultaneous S20\u2013S13 cable failure without multiple independent disconnections.", "grounded": ["oms.S20-S01"], "n_grounded": 1, "note": ""}], "probability_other": 0.03, "sum_stated": 0.97}, "llm": {"provider": "openai", "model": "gpt-5.6"}, "llm_calls": [{"role": "proposer", "latency_s": 31.65186095237732, "input_tokens": 19670, "output_tokens": 2542, "reasoning_tokens": 2030, "ok": true, "error": ""}]}